            <div xml:id="d247">

                <pb facs="0345" n="243" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg243"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/6071: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Tientsin (Lockhart) to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tientsin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-03-20T12:00:00+08:00">March 20,
                        1933—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received March 20—4:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>General Yao Tung-fang has relieved General Ho Chu-kuo as commanding officer in
                    Chinwangtao area. General Ho and his troops, who have been at Chinwangtao for
                    several months, are being moved to Lwanchow.</p>
                <p>General Han Fu-chu passed through Tientsin yesterday from Shantung to Peiping en
                    route Paotingfu for conference with Chiang Kai-shek. Unconfirmed reports have
                    been current for several days that Han may assume command of Chiang’s forces in
                    North China in the near future.</p>
                <p>Both sides still claiming Hsifengkou.</p>
                <p>Situation Tientsin quiet.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
